  "question_stem": "{{figure:diagram_q07_01.png}}\nTwo particles $P$ and $Q$ of masses $0.5\\text{ kg}$ and $m\\text{ kg}$ respectively are attached to the ends of a light inextensible string. The string passes over a fixed smooth pulley which is attached to the top of two inclined planes. The particles are initially at rest with $P$ on a smooth plane inclined at $30^{\\circ}$ to the horizontal and $Q$ on a plane inclined at $45^{\\circ}$ to the horizontal. The string is taut and the particles can move on lines of greatest slope of the two planes. A force of magnitude $0.8\\text{ N}$ is applied to $P$ acting down the plane, causing $P$ to move down the plane (see diagram).",
